    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40810" root="هب" body-key="h">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِبَّةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبَّةٌ</span> throughout. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>A state,</i> or <i>condition:</i> [or perhaps the meaning intended is the
<i>state of being brisk, lively,</i> or <i>sprightly, and quick</i>].
(K.) Ex. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَّهُ لَحَسَنُ الهِبَّةِ</span> <i>Verily he is in a good
state,</i> or <i>condition, &amp;c.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِبَّةٌ</span> The <i>state</i>
of a stallion <i>when excited by desire of the female.</i>
(S.) See 1. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِبَّةٌ</span> <i>A piece of a garment,</i> or <i>the
like:</i> (K:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِبْبٌ</span>, (S, K:) <i>a piece of rag.</i>
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَوْبٌ هَبَائِبُ</span>.

